sql/1.0.0/rules.sql:10:1: warning: bad_target(code) references parent(code), which is neither its primary key nor a unique key; SQLite refuses writes to bad_target with "foreign key mismatch" [fk_target]
sql/1.0.0/rules.sql:33:1: warning: descpk.id is INTEGER PRIMARY KEY DESC, which SQLite does not make the rowid; drop DESC [pk_shape]
sql/1.0.0/rules.sql:28:1: warning: lax is not STRICT [strict]
sql/1.0.0/rules.sql:20:1: warning: link(b) references parent, but no index of link starts with (b); deleting from parent scans link [fk_indexed]
sql/1.0.0/rules.sql:26:1: warning: unique key loose(email) holds nullable email; SQLite treats NULLs as distinct, so any number of rows may share it [nullable_unique]
sql/1.0.0/rules.sql:38:1: warning: no_created has no created_at column [created_at]
sql/1.0.0/rules.sql:31:1: warning: nopk has no primary key; it needs an INTEGER PRIMARY KEY that is its rowid [pk_shape]
sql/1.0.0/rules.sql:39:1: warning: only_updated has no created_at column [created_at]
sql/1.0.0/rules.sql:39:1: warning: only_updated has updated_at but no created_at [updated_at_needs_created_at]
sql/1.0.0/rules.sql:17:1: warning: orphan(other) references nowhere, which does not exist [fk_target]
sys.sql:2:1: warning: plain_meta is created by the system-tables script but does not start with sys_ [prefix_origin]
sql/1.0.0/rules.sql:41:1: warning: stamps.created_at matches '*_at' but is declared 'TEXT', which is not an integer type [stamp_type]
sql/1.0.0/rules.sql:41:1: warning: stamps.seen_at matches '*_at' but is declared 'REAL', which is not an integer type [stamp_type]
sql/1.0.0/rules.sql:43:1: warning: sys_rogue starts with sys_, which is reserved for tables the system-tables script creates [prefix_origin]
sql/1.0.0/rules.sql:32:1: warning: the primary key twokey(a, b) has 2 columns; it needs to be one INTEGER PRIMARY KEY that is the rowid [pk_shape]
sql/1.0.0/rules.sql:30:1: warning: wr is not STRICT [strict]
sql/1.0.0/rules.sql:30:1: warning: wr is WITHOUT ROWID; it needs an INTEGER PRIMARY KEY that is its rowid [pk_shape]
sql/1.0.0/rules.sql:36:1: warning: wrong_id.serial is the primary key without AUTOINCREMENT, so it should be named id [pk_naming]
sql/1.0.0/rules.sql:35:1: warning: wrong_serial.id is the primary key with AUTOINCREMENT, so it should be named serial [pk_naming]
